            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0519" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-22T12:00:00+08:00">February 22,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 22—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>261. Following from American Consul General, Mukden.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“February 20, 6 p.m. According to a report of the Japanese press,
                        preparations for the establishment of the new state are being carried out
                        rapidly and its inauguration will occur at Changchun on March 1st. The
                        report also said that Changchun will be the capital and that work on the
                        buildings for the new government has been started. It is reported Pu Yi will be the President.”</p></quote>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
